# Financial Text Topic Modelling

An end-to-end Natural Language Processing (NLP) pipeline and interactive **Streamlit** web application for discovering latent topics in financial news and text documents using **Gensim Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA)**.

## Overview

Financial headlines, market commentary, and news snippets span dozens of recurring themes—such as earnings, central bank policy, mergers & acquisitions, commodities, and market movements. This project preprocesses financial text, trains an LDA topic model on the `zeroshot/twitter-financial-news-topic` dataset, evaluates topic coherence ($C_v$), and provides a Streamlit interface for exploring topics and assigning topics to new documents.

## Repository Structure

```text
financial-text-topic-modelling/
├── app.py                  # Streamlit web GUI
├── src/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── preprocess.py           # Text cleaning & tokenization for LDA
│   └── train_lda.py            # Dataset loading, LDA training & coherence evaluation
├── data/                   # Sample datasets for testing
├── models/                 # Saved Gensim LDA model & dictionary
├── screenshots/            # Working Streamlit GUI screenshots
├── requirements.txt        # Python dependencies
├── .gitignore
└── README.md


Setup & Installation

Clone the repository:

Bash

git clone [https://github.com/haru-6/financial-text-topic-modelling.git](https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/financial-text-topic-modelling.git)
cd financial-text-topic-modelling
Create and activate a virtual environment (Python 3.12 recommended for gensim compatibility):

Bash

py -3.12 -m venv .venv312
.venv312\Scripts\Activate.ps1
Install dependencies:

Bash

pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt



Usage


1. Train the LDA Topic Model

Run the training script to clean the dataset, build the dictionary/corpus, train the LDA model, and log topic coherence (𝐶𝑣):

Bash

python src/train_lda.py



2. Launch the Streamlit Web App


Bash

streamlit run app.py



In the web interface, you can:

Upload a dataset/file or use sample financial text.

Run topic modelling and inspect discovered topics along with their top keywords/weights and coherence score (𝐶𝑣).

View document-to-topic assignments, distribution charts, and filter/download results.



